# Conformance fixture evidence: one small .mgcr per fixture
# (docs/CONFORMANCE.md), committed via git-lfs so the suite travels
# with the repo. The nested glob matches the per-take directories
# (conformance/fixtures/<take>/t<tick>-<law>.mgcr).
#
# What changed vs the old one-bundle-per-take shape is the WRITE
# PATTERN, not the storage: a bundle was re-frozen whenever its fixture
# set changed, minting a fresh permanent 14-43 MB object every time (18
# versions, 178 MB, for 10 live bundles). Per-fixture files are
# write-once — the evidence never changes after it is cut, and the
# mutable verdict (status/sig/note) lives in the manifest TEXT — so
# appending costs one ~20 KB blob and nothing is ever rewritten. These
# are zstd frames, which never delta-compress in a packfile, so keeping
# them out of it is the right call as the corpus grows.
#
# Fullsize recordings still never enter git (/recordings is ignored).
conformance/fixtures/**/*.mgcr filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
